---
title: MLS group and epoch lifecycle
---
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Genesis: relay provisioned, genesis key created

  Genesis --> RootEpoch0: bootstrap invite redeemed<br/>first device self-admits as trust root and admin
  note right of Genesis
    The genesis key signs exactly one bootstrap invite
    and is destroyed on redemption. There is no reissue.
  end note

  state RootEpoch0 {
    [*] --> Stable
    Stable --> Committing: member add / remove / update / rekey
    Committing --> Stable: epoch advances, new epoch secret derived
  }

  RootEpoch0 --> WorkspaceRoot: roster document established

  state WorkspaceRoot {
    [*] --> Active
    Active --> Active: roster.update (0x0020)
    Active --> Revoking: roster.revoke (0x0021)
    Revoking --> Active: epoch advance ENFORCES the revocation
    Active --> RecoveryWrapped: recovery.wrap (0x0061) per recovery principal per epoch<br/>stored under a per-epoch blinded tag
    RecoveryWrapped --> Active
    Active --> DirectoryUpdate: recovery.directory (0x0063)<br/>current, candidate, fallback tags bound to a target commit
    DirectoryUpdate --> Active
  }

  WorkspaceRoot --> ChannelGroup: channel created, enrolment key<br/>exported from the parent epoch secret

  state ChannelGroup {
    [*] --> Published
    Published --> Published: groupinfo.publish (0x0060)<br/>relay keeps only the latest per group
    Published --> SelfJoined: member external-commits using that GroupInfo
    SelfJoined --> Published: republished by whichever member committed
    Published --> PendingAdd: target device out of key packages<br/>or its packages expired past 90 days
    PendingAdd --> Published: device tops back up to the 20 target
  }

  state HistoryPolicy <<choice>>
  ChannelGroup --> HistoryPolicy
  HistoryPolicy --> OpenHistory: policy = open
  HistoryPolicy --> ClosedHistory: policy = closed

  OpenHistory: history.publish (0x0062)<br/>historical epoch secrets sealed to the long-lived history key,<br/>that key wrapped under the parent-derived enrolment key
  ClosedHistory: joiner reads from its joining epoch forward only

  OpenHistory --> Compaction
  ClosedHistory --> Compaction

  Compaction: checkpoint (0x0071) signed manifest.<br/>Author barriers, index snapshot, every document snapshot/head.<br/>Server-side pruning is a separate signed operation, never a relay decision.
  Compaction --> WorkspaceRoot

  WorkspaceRoot --> AgentLeaf: agent certificate issued by a device
  AgentLeaf: Holds no MLS state, never opens a socket.<br/>Never an expected attester. Its issuing device attests on its behalf.
  AgentLeaf --> WorkspaceRoot: agent leaf eviction, epoch advance

  WorkspaceRoot --> Offboarded: offboarding as ONE action
  Offboarded: removal plus the epoch change that enforces it.<br/>Removed members cannot decrypt post-removal epochs.
  Offboarded --> [*]

  WorkspaceRoot --> Compromised: key compromise declared
  Compromised --> WorkspaceRoot: full rekey, recovery wraps reissued for the new epoch
